WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.752
Unit ten: This/That/These/Those. Today you will point to things that are near and far.

4
00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:17.693
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:21.866
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.578
This.

7
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:26.548
This means one thing that is near you.

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.523
This is my pen.

9
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.339
Your turn. Say: This.

10
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.004
This.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.577
That.

12
00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:39.803
That means one thing that is far from you.

13
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.708
That is a tall tree.

14
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:44.841
Your turn. Say: That.

15
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.353
That.

16
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:49.816
These.

17
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.153
These means more than one thing that is near you.

18
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.088
These are my books.

19
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:58.185
Your turn. Say: These.

20
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.011
These.

21
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.751
Those.

22
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.191
Those means more than one thing that is far from you.

23
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.191
Those are mountains.

24
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:12.320
Your turn. Say: Those.

25
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.005
Those.

26
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.472
Near.

27
00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:20.251
Near means not far away.

28
00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.583
The school is near my house.

29
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.383
Your turn. Say: Near.

30
00:01:28.233 --> 00:01:29.095
Near.

31
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.526
Far.

32
00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:33.365
Far means a long way away.

33
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.590
The sea is far from here.

34
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:38.429
Your turn. Say: Far.

35
00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.036
Far.

36
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:43.819
Singular.

37
00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:46.723
Singular means one only.

38
00:01:47.317 --> 00:01:48.945
This is a singular noun.

39
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.086
Your turn. Say: Singular.

40
00:01:54.933 --> 00:01:56.016
Singular.

41
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.403
Plural.

42
00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.080
Plural means more than one.

43
00:02:00.683 --> 00:02:02.230
These are plural nouns.

44
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:05.063
Your turn. Say: Plural.

45
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:08.646
Plural.

46
00:02:09.433 --> 00:02:13.293
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.988
Visal, point to your pen. What do you say?

48
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:26.880
I say This is my pen. We use this for one thing that is near. For one thing that is far, we say that: That is a tall tree.

49
00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:29.449
And for many things?

50
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:38.555
We use these for plural things near us: These are my books. We use those for plural things far away: Those are mountains.

51
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:41.150
Is there a simple rule?

52
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:54.419
This and these are near. That and those are far. This and that are singular. These and those are plural. Use is with singular and are with plural.

53
00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.264
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.117 --> 00:03:01.544
Grammar focus: This and that and these and those.

55
00:03:01.844 --> 00:03:03.124
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:05.096
This is my pen.

57
00:03:05.983 --> 00:03:07.286
That is a tall tree.

58
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:09.417
These are my books.

59
00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:17.213
This and these are for things that are near. That and those are for things that are far. This and that are singular; these and those are plural.

60
00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.276
Be careful! Don't say: These is my book.

61
00:03:23.233 --> 00:03:25.546
Say: This is my book.

62
00:03:25.846 --> 00:03:27.602
Use this with one near thing.

63
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.482
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.639
Near and Far.

65
00:03:33.939 --> 00:03:36.508
This is my desk, and these are my books.

66
00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.394
That is the teacher's desk, and those are her pencils.

67
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.759
The window is far, but the board is near.

68
00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.859
A singular noun means one thing.

69
00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:50.261
A plural noun means more than one thing.

70
00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:55.125
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:55.983 --> 00:03:58.253
blank is my bag. (near, one)

72
00:03:58.553 --> 00:04:01.800
A, This. B, These. C, Those.

73
00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:07.205
The answer is A: This.

74
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.921
blank are my shoes. (near, many)

75
00:04:11.221 --> 00:04:14.549
A, That. B, Those. C, These.

76
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.494
The answer is C: These.

77
00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.861
blank is a mountain. (far, one)

78
00:04:24.161 --> 00:04:26.967
A, That. B, Those. C, These.

79
00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:32.185
The answer is A: That.

80
00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.966
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:35.266 --> 00:04:40.104
A, These is my pen.. B, Those are far.. C, This are my books..

82
00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.212
The answer is B: Those are far..

83
00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.371
According to the reading, what are on the teacher's desk?

84
00:04:50.671 --> 00:04:54.917
A, her pencils. B, my books. C, my bags.

85
00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:00.710
The answer is A: her pencils.

86
00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.831
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:05.683 --> 00:05:09.529
Point to something near you and something far away, and describe each one.

88
00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.863
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:20.163 --> 00:05:32.144
This is my pencil, and it is near me. That is a tree outside the window, and it is far from me. I use this and that for one thing. I use these and those for more than one thing.

90
00:05:32.444 --> 00:05:34.176
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:40.058
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and this and that and these and those.

92
00:05:40.358 --> 00:05:44.101
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:05:44.401 --> 00:05:46.717
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

94
00:05:47.017 --> 00:05:49.669
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

